  "notes": "WRITING:\nOften written in kana, こす, because {漉|こ} is not in the standard-use (⟦{常用|じょうよう}→常用：32069_jouyou⟧) kanji list.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- ⟦{布|ぬの}→布：01489_nuno⟧⟦で→で：00502_de⟧{漉|こ}す: to strain through cloth\n- ざる⟦で→で：00502_de⟧{漉|こ}す: to strain through a colander\n- だし⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{漉|こ}す: to strain stock\n- ⟦{裏漉|うらご}し→裏漉し：23464_uragoshi⟧: pressing through a fine sieve (noun)\n\nWATCH OUT:\n- ⟦{越|こ}す→越す：02282_kosu⟧ (to cross, to pass) and ⟦{超|こ}す→超す：02465_kosu⟧ (to exceed) are different words with the same reading\n- The same kanji writes {漉|す}く, to make paper by hand (⟦{紙|かみ}→紙：00712_kami⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{漉|す}く)",
